<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pernīcĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		pernix, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>nimbleness</i>, <i>briskness</i>, <i>agility</i>, <i>swiftness</i>, <i>fleetness</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pernicitas deserit: consitus sum senectute,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Men. 5, 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adde pernicitatem et velocitatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 15, 45</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 3, 84</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedum pernicitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
					16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines saltatim currentes, vivacissimae
					pernicitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					9, 4, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					1, 79</span></i>
			.</div>
